        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+===========================================================================+\n|                  GLOBAL FRESHWATER — SUPPLY, DEMAND, AND CRISIS           |\n+===========================================================================+\n|                                                                           |\n|  SUPPLY (fixed on century timescale):                                     |\n|  Global renewable freshwater: ~42,750 km³/yr (river discharge)            |\n|  Accessible (excluding flood pulse, remote regions): ~12,500 km³/yr       |\n|  Geographically concentrated: 60% in 9 countries                         |\n|                                                                           |\n|  DEMAND (growing):                                                        |\n|  Global freshwater withdrawal ~4,000 km³/yr (2020)                       |\n|  Agriculture: ~70%; Industry: ~20%; Municipal: ~10%                      |\n|  Consumptive use: ~2,500 km³/yr (50% withdrawn, not returned)            |\n|                                                                           |\n|  TREND:                                                                   |\n|  Growing population + urbanization + climate change                      |\n|  → demand rising, supply increasingly variable                            |\n|  → 4 billion people experience severe water scarcity ≥1 month/year        |\n|  → 500 million face year-round severe scarcity                            |\n+===========================================================================+\n```"
    },
